    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py:1506-1507 calls `plain_writer_launch(Path.cwd(), args.provider)`. Its first statement (lines ~276-278) calls `worker_credentials.llm_env(...)` outside the inner `launch`. A worker started with `--kinds repair,review --provider claude` therefore reads the token file even if it only ever claims a review job. A CredentialError there exits with code 2. The design says a kind that starts no provider never reads the token file, but this is only enforced by the kinds set, not per job. Deferring the call into `launch` would match the per-job behaviour.",
      "id": "eager-writer-credential-resolution",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The plain writer launch resolves the Claude credential once at worker start, not when a write-kind job is claimed. On an operator node with a bad token file, a worker started with `--run --llm-command` fails before any job is claimed."
    }
